 ### Simplex Noise 3D Gradient
-Simplex Noise 3D Gradient computes the 3D Simplex Noise value and its spatial gradient (derivative) simultaneously [S7, unofficial]. It performs the same skewing, corner identification, and surflet coordinate calculations as standard Simplex Noise 3D [S7, unofficial]. It computes contribution weights $t_m = \max(0.6 - \mathbf{x}_m \cdot \mathbf{x}_m, 0)$ and gradient vectors $\mathbf{g}_m$ for each corner [S7, unofficial]. The derivative is calculated as $\mathbf{deriv} = -8 \sum t_{m,2} \mathbf{x}_m (\mathbf{g}_m \cdot \mathbf{x}_m) + \sum t_{m,4} \mathbf{g}_m$, where $t_{m,2} = t_m^2$ and $t_{m,4} = t_m^4$ [S7, unofficial]. The result is returned as a vector containing the noise value scaled by 46.0 and the gradient scaled by 7.4 [S7, unofficial].
